%N A398615 Decimal expansion of the long/short edge length ratio of a canonical (dual-uniform) 9-gonal trapezohedron.
%C A398615 The 9-gonal trapezohedron is the dual polyhedron of the 9-gonal antiprism.
%H A398615 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A398615/b398615.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398615 Polytope Wiki, <a href="https://polytope.miraheze.org/wiki/Enneagonal_antitegum">Enneagonal antitegum</a>.
%H A398615 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Trapezohedron.html">Trapezohedron</a>.
%H A398615 <a href="/index/Al#algebraic_03">Index entries for algebraic numbers, degree 3</a>.
%F A398615 Equals (csc(Pi/18)^2)/4.
%F A398615 Equals the largest root of x^3 - 9*x^2 + 6*x - 1.
%e A398615 8.2908593693815896066212224104097592276164974512186...
%t A398615 First[RealDigits[Csc[Pi/18]^2/4, 10, 100]]
%t A398615 (* Alternative: *)
%t A398615 First[RealDigits[Max[PolyhedronData[{"Trapezohedron", 9}, "EdgeLengths"]], 10, 100]]
